<title>USA: US Comptroller names senior deputy for supervision.</title>
<headline>US Comptroller names senior deputy for supervision.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Comptroller Eugene Ludwig named Wayne Rushton as senior deputy comptroller for bank supervision, the Comptroller's office said on Friday.</p>
<p>Rushton, who has worked at the Comptroller's office since 1965, will be responsible for formulating and implementing safety and soundness policies and procedures for national banks and bank examiners.</p>
<p>The appointment takes effect on May 5, the comptroller's office said. The post was previously held by Susan Krause, who became senior deputy comptroller for international affairs in March.</p>
<p>--Aaron Pressman((202-898-8312))</p>
